<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Quick Settings tile badge: Clash-Flux paw mark.

  Two files, one per shade theme:
    * drawable/ic_qs_clash_flux.xml       - black paw, for a light shade
    * drawable-night/ic_qs_clash_flux.xml - white paw, for a dark shade

  Why the viewport is 1200x1565 (portrait) instead of square:
  SystemUI does NOT fit tile icons uniformly. Measured on ColorOS 15
  (Android 15, OnePlus PJE110) the 40dp square drawable was stretched
  into a ~24.67 x 32.18dp box (fitXY, 1.304x vertical stretch). The paw
  silhouette is vertically extended in the path transform so it stays
  nearly square in that measured box instead of looking flattened.

  On a ROM that fits the icon uniformly (FIT_CENTER) this drawable stays
  undistorted too, only marginally smaller than a square one; the trade-off is
  that a ROM stretching a square box would stretch this one the other way.

  Intrinsic width stays 40dp so the badge keeps the size the previous mascot
  badge had; the artwork has a small vertical safety margin for the tile mask.
-->
